.TH CMP 1 "October 25, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
cmp \- compare two files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmp
.RB [ \-l | \-s ]
.I file1 file2
.SH DESCRIPTION
The two files are compared for identical contents.
By default, a discrepancy is noted by giving the first differing byte
number and line number, both counted from 1.
If one file is a prefix of the other, an end-of-file diagnostic is printed.
.TP
.B \-l
List every differing byte: decimal position and the two octal byte values.
.TP
.B \-s
Suppress ordinary difference reports. Open and usage errors still appear.
.PP
The two options are mutually exclusive.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/CMP  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
diff(1), comm(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 for identical files, 1 for different files, 2 for a usage or open error.
.SH BUGS
The byte position and line counters are 24-bit, which is exact for every file maux can open (a file's length is a 3-byte field, at most 16,777,215 bytes).
